Tell that to a Zen Samurai.  :-)  

It is possible for the message to be wiped out before you see it.  Not
very likely, but possible.  Best practice, never kick down a door to get
into a room.  If you absolutely must kick down a door (rare, but
sometimes necessary), do it from inside the room.  If you're actually 
at a point where the only way to proceed is to kick down a door in a 
hallway, and there's no way some monster is going to do it for you, 
and you can't dig or go down a trap door or a hole, then you should at
least be aware of whether there is a shop on your level, through
auditory clues.  If there IS a shop, it behooves you to try to find it 
first.  There's always the possibility that behind the locked door is
the other shop on that level :-)

The fact is, it's almost never necessary to kick down a door.  It's
almost always safe to do so (but I don't like waking up monsters), but
when it's not safe, it's often YASD, so it deserves careful
consideration.  I think it's a good effect, for those characters who 
storm through the dungeon kicking down doors as the normal route,
without even checking whether they are locked or not.



